   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hi all, is there a way of plotting abundance and CI estimated by a distance sampling model?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Thanks a lot.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Cheers,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Joaquin</div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Joaquín Aldabe</b><br><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"Arial, sans-serif\" color=\"#1155cc\"><br></font><font size=\"2\">Departamento de Sistemas Agrarios y Paisajes Culturales<br>Centro Universitario de la Región Este, Universidad de la República, Uruguay<br></font><div><font size=\"2\">Ruta 15 (y Ruta 9), Km 28.500, Departamento de Rocha  </font></div><div><font size=\"2\">                                                           </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ee\"><u><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/joaquin-aldabe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sites.google.com/view/joaquin-aldabe&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473497755000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NvylnacfglxYhi0lTWbfj\">https://sites.google.com/view/joaquin-aldabe</a></u></font><br></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "reYG4u1qBwAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "f2122b34f1aa6e95",
   "date": "2020-03-30T07:33:52Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Plot abunance estimate",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">Joaquín:</font></font></span></div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">There is not a function in the Distance package for plotting estimates and confidence intervals from a fitted model.  I suspect you are interested in plotting a set of estimates derived from a number of strata or a number of surveys.</font></font></span></div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">You should be able to make progress with plotting if you understand the structure of the object created by a call to </font></font></span><code><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">ds()</font></font></span></code><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\"> .</font></font></span></div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">I have an example where I&#39;ve created an object </font></font></span><code><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\">wren</font></font></span></code><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><font style=\"font-family:system-ui\"> from fitting a detection function to point transect data.  The point estimate of abundance of individuals (and the bounds of the confidence interval) are within that object:</font></font></span></div><br><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\">&gt;str(wren$dht$individuals$N)\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\">&#39;data.frame&#39;:\t1 obs. of  7 variables:\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ Label   : Factor w/ 1 level &quot;Total&quot;: 1\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ Estimate: num 33.7\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ se      : num 19.6\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ cv      : num 0.584\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ lcl     : num 11.5\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ ucl     : num 98.3\r\n</span></font></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:monospace\"><font style=\"font-size:13.02px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,114,120)\"> $ df      : num 120</span></font></font></div><br><div>Let me know if you need more information to produce your plots.</div><br><div><u></u><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1px\"></td><td><div><strong>Eric Rexstad</strong></div><div>Senior Research Fellow, CREEM, Univ. of St Andrews, Charity SC013532</div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><div style=\"font-size:0.9em;border-top:1px dashed gray;min-width:250px;max-width:400px;margin-top:10px;padding-top:4px\"><div><a style=\"margin-right:8px\" href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">eric.r...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a><a style=\"margin-right:8px\" href=\"tel:+44%20(0)1334%20461833\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+44 (0)1334 461833</a></div><div><a style=\"margin-right:8px\" href=\"http://erex.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://erex.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473497757000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WE9OknOC9oEkv5KR-m89T\">http://erex.github.io</a></div><div><a href=\"https://maps.google.com/?q=The%20Observatory%2C%20Buchanan%20Gardens%2C%20St%20Andrews%20KY16%209LZ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://maps.google.com/?q%3DThe%2520Observatory%252C%2520Buchanan%2520Gardens%252C%2520St%2520Andrews%2520KY16%25209LZ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473497757000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Mmw_jRpd-5bMvA2RGOjHf\">The Observatory, Buchanan Gardens, St Andrews KY16 9LZ</a></div></div></td></tr></tbody></table><u></u></div>"
